  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Chinese owners have committed the Kamsarmax \"Nova Optimus\" 81/2012 Jiangsu, China (SS 09/2027, DD 12/2025, BWTS fitted) to clients of Fujian Haitong at mid USD 16 mill. Remind you that the sister vessel \"Theresa Guangdong\" 81/2012 Jiangsu, China (SS 05/2027, DD 09/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in August at USD 19,2 mill. The Ultramax \"Scorpio WQ\" 76/2004 Sasebo, Japan (SS 02/2029, DD 07/2026, BWTS fitted) was committed at region USD 10,6 mill, while the one-year-younger \"HC Victory\" 75/2005 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed at USD 10,5 mill. For reference, the \"Bravery\" 76/2004 Imabari, Japan (SS 06/2027, DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in May at region USD 12 mill. Oldendorff Carriers committed their Ultramax \"Alwine Oldendorff\" 61/2014 JMU, Japan (SS/DD 12/2024, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) & \"August Oldendorff\" 61/2015 JMU, Japan (SS/DD 01/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) were committed to Greek interests at USD 50,5 mill enbloc. Note that earlier this month, the \"Lowlands Amstel\" 61/2015 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at low-mid USD 26 mill. On the Supramax sector, the \"Virono Pride\" 58/2009 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 01/2027, DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed to Chinese interests at low-mid USD 15 mill. Remind you that a month ago, the sister vessel \"Titan I\" 58/2009 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS/DD 11/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 16 mill. Moreover, Spar Shipping committed their \"Spar Spica\" 53/2005 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 01/2025, BWTS fitted) at region USD 10,5 mill, while the sister vessel \"Spar Lyra\" 53/2005 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 10/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold back in July at USD 10,2 mill. Japanese owners committed their Handysize \"Ken Mei\" 29/2003 Shikoku, Japan (SS 09/2028, DD 10/2026, BWTS fitted) at USD 7,3 mill and the two- years-younger sister vessel \"Ken Toku\" 29/2005 Shikoku, Japan (SS/DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) at mid USD 8 mill. Note that the sister vessel \"Ken Hou\" 29/2004 Shikoku, Japan (SS/DD 11/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold back in July at USD 8,6 mill.",
    "tankers": "",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 11,000/13,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 11,000/14,000 pd. South African trips into India were fixed around usd 12,000/13,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 200K/300K. Continental trips via US East Coast into Atlantic were reported at the level of usd 10,000/11,000 pd. US Gulf trips into China were fixed around usd 15,000/16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K/600K. US Gulf trips into South America were reported at the level of usd 18,000/20,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 19,000/20,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 13,000/15,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 300K/500K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 15,000 pd for 5/7 months employment basis delivery Japan.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 12,000/15,000 pd. Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Indian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 9,000/12,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips into East Coast India were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. West African trips into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000/17,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from China via Indonesia into Continent were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. South African trips into East Africa were fixed around usd 7,000/9,000 pd. South African trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 11,000/13,000 pd. Continental and Mediterranean trips into West Africa were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Continent trips into USG-USEC range were reported at the level of usd 10,000/13,000 pd. Inter- Mediterranean trips via Black Sea were fixed around usd 9,000/11,000 pd. US Gulf trips into South America were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. US Gulf trips into West Africa were fixed around usd 15,000/18,000 pd. Trips from US East Coast into Japan were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. North Coast South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 14,000/15,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
